# Mapper mappings

Do not add custom MapStruct mappings (`@Mapping`, `@Mappings`, `@AfterMapping`, `expression`, `qualifiedBy`, or a hand-written mapping method) unless the user has agreed in this conversation.

Name source and target properties the same so MapStruct maps them with a plain method (`toResponse(Source source)`). If that is not enough, stop and ask. Prefer a simpler model or API shape over a custom mapping.

```java
// ❌ BAD — custom mapping added without asking
@Mapping(target = "basePaymentPlan.type", source = "basePaymentPlanType")
ClassroomResponse toResponse(Classroom classroom);

// ✅ GOOD — same property names, no @Mapping
ClassroomResponse toResponse(Classroom classroom);
```
